{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver did not give the notice POL-RD-21 requires before or at the point of deviation. The chat log carries exactly two messages, both sent before the trip began (20:38:52 and 20:39:12) and both about the pickup point — 'At Dempsey Block 8 drop off' and 'ok' — and the trip record's own POL-RD-21 field, derived.v7.messages_during_trip, is an empty list, with in_app_calls also empty. The deviation was detected at 20:54:05, some fourteen minutes after the trip started, so nothing was sent 'before or at the point of deviation' and the notification duty is unmet.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05017", "EV-TRIP-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's case rests on a bare verbal notice — his own filing asks 'Telling verbally also counts right?'. POL-RD-21 allows verbal notice only 'with the trip call recording as evidence', and the record contains no call recording: in_app_calls is empty on the trip record, and the clause's own note records that the records carry no call recordings at all. A verbal notice with no recording in the record cannot be established, and the clause's confirmation test — whether the chat log or a call recording confirms the rider's acknowledgment — is not met, so this is not an agreed deviation and the rider's on-file account that he was told nothing is left standing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05017", "EV-CHAT-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is over tolerance, which closes the only rows that would leave the 0.86 SGD with the driver. POL-RD-22 measures the deviation from the platform's recorded distances — 13.2 km actual minus 12.0 km recommended = 1.20 km — against a 1.0 km tolerance, and 1.20 km exceeds it. Rows (c) and (e) of POL-RD-24 (within tolerance, no refund) therefore cannot apply, and the driver cannot get the money back on a tolerance argument.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Traffic justification is not established either. POL-RD-23 requires a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY that intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window; the only advisory in the record, EV-ADVIS-05017-01, reports its own intersects_route field as undetermined — 'the record does not say whether this advisory lies on the recommended route' — and leaves justifies_reroute to the Judge. An advisory whose overlap with the recommended route is not shown cannot satisfy the intersect requirement of POL-RD-23, so the reroute is not made out as traffic-justified and row (d) of POL-RD-24 applies.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05017-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-05017-01.payload.derived.v7.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the driver's most favourable account — that an accident on the CTE made the Braddell Road exit reasonable — the highest row he can reach is row (b), not row (a). Under POL-RD-24(a) a traffic-justified deviation escapes refund only if the rider was informed and agreed, and POL-RD-21 supplies the only proof of agreement: confirmation in the chat log or in a call recording. Neither exists. The agreed-deviation route to no refund is shut on this record, and the refund in row (b) is due.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05017-01", "EV-CHAT-05017", "EV-TRIP-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-RD-21"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "It makes no difference to the rider which of the two open rows applies, because both pay the same sum and pay it to the rider. POL-RD-24 computes the refund as deviation distance times the per-km rate without surge — 1.20 km x 0.72 SGD = 0.86 SGD — and EV-FARE-05017 records exactly that: excess_distance_fare_sgd 0.86, refund_issued_sgd 0.86, payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED. So whether the case is row (b) or row (d), the 0.86 SGD is the rider's, and nothing in POL-RD-24 moves any part of it back to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05017", "EV-TRIP-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-FARE-05017.payload.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The case is ruleable now, and escalation would leave the driver in no better position. The deviation is 1.20 km, inside POL-RD-25's 2.0 km AI limit; the contested value is 0.86 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD line, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence; neither profile carries a fraud flag (fraud_flags 0 on both); no safety indicator appears; and every artifact cited is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so POL-GEN-02's confidence cap does not bite. The single undetermined item — whether the advisory intersects the recommended route — cannot change the result, because rows (b) and (d) both refund the excess distance fare; there is no open question that needs a human to resolve.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05017", "EV-ADVIS-05017-01", "EV-RPROF-05017", "EV-DPROF-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-25", "POL-GEN-22", "POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The filing party is the driver, and the present state already takes the 0.86 SGD off his earnings and leaves it with the rider (fare_adjusted at 2026-09-10T03:30:02). POL-GEN-03 reads the outcome from the filer's claim against that state: because the driver's claim is not supported on this record, no sum is owed to him and the outcome is NO_ACTION — the present state stands, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both null.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05017", "EV-TRIP-05017"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the driver and the rider: The trip record shows actual distance 13.2 km against a recommended 12.0 km, so the deviation is 1.20 km, over the 1.0 km tolerance. The LTA advisory (ACCIDENT on CTE towards SLE after Braddell Road exit, valid 20:23-21:40) covers the trip window and the CTE segment of the recommended route, so I accept the driver's point that the reroute was traffic-justified under POL-RD-23. However, the question whether the driver notified the rider cannot be established. POL-RD-21 requires notice by in-app chat or verbally with a call recording; the chat log has only two pre-trip messages about the pickup point, and the trip record's in_app_calls is empty. The driver's verbal notice has no recording, and POL-RD-21 provides that such notice cannot be established. Since POL-GEN-26 names 'whether the driver notified the rider' as a fact that must be established, and POL-RD-24 has no row for a traffic-justified deviation over 1 km where notification is unestablished, the case must go to a human reviewer. I therefore reject the rider's argument that row (b) applies: the record does not establish that the rider was not informed, only that notification cannot be established. The 0.86 SGD already refunded (1.20 km x 0.72 SGD/km) is held pending review. No safety or fraud flags apply, and no route-deviation referral clause exists."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
